WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:04.779
If you like your laughs with a splash of the
red stuff, chances are you can already quote

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:09.120
every line from Fargo, accent and all, and
you think about Heathers whenever you get

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.120
a slushie.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.780
"Our love is God.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.680
Let's go get a slushie."

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:20.500
While plenty of dark comedies are bonafide
classics, there are a slew of other nuanced,

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.840
hilarious, and joyfully destructive movies
that may have slipped under your radar.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.180
Here are some lesser known dark comedies that'll
have you laughing the pain away.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.640
Arsenic and Old Lace

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:35.790
It's a classic of the subgenre, but many younger
movie-lovers have missed out on the incredible

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:39.010
1944 dark comedy Arsenic and Old Lace.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:43.879
The movie stars Cary Grant as Mortimer Brewster,
a pretty normal guy who is shocked to learn

00:00:43.879 --> 00:00:49.030
that his two elderly aunts have developed
a nasty habit of slaying all of their gentlemen

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:50.030
callers.

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:53.890
"You think my aunts are sweet, charming old
ladies, don't you?

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:56.220
Well, there's 13 bodies buried in the cellar."

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.220
"Mmmmmnmm!"

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.780
The movie, which is based on the play of the
same name by Joseph Kesselring, is entirely

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:06.860
bizarre from start to finish, with pitch-black
jokes that still hold up today.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:10.790
While the Brewster family is definitely not
one you'd want to be a part of, their lethal

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:13.320
antics make for timeless dark comedy.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:13.860
"The gentleman died because he drank some
wine with poison in it."

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:14.860
Barton Fink

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:19.060
"The important thing is: we all want it to
have that Barton Fink feeling.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:22.850
I guess we all have that Barton Fink feeling,
but since you're Barton Fink I'm assuming

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.380
you have it in spades."

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:28.230
The Coen brothers have written and directed
several classic dark comedies, and although

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:32.930
you've likely seen many of their films, there
are still some hidden gems in their filmography.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:38.359
This includes the hauntingly surreal 1991
film Barton Fink, which features John Turturro

00:01:38.359 --> 00:01:42.820
as a playwright who discovers the seedy side
of Hollywood when he takes a job writing for

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:43.820
a movie studio.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:47.990
As Turturro's Barton Fink quickly learns,
the hotel he is staying at is more than just

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:53.060
a dump — it's also home to a brutal madman
who seems to be targeting people close to

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.060
Barton.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:59.030
John Goodman stars in the film as Fink's,
uhh, "unique" neighbor, while Tony Shalhoub

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.100
also makes an early career appearance.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:06.500
Less a bloodbath like Fargo and lacking the
laugh out loud sensibilities of The Big Lebowski,

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:10.959
Barton Fink is a comedic — and yet deadly
serious — tale of writer's block and the

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:12.950
classic Faustian bargain.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:16.280
In other words: it's a thinking man's dark
comedy.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.400
In Bruges

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:22.480
Colin Farrell is a hitman with a conscience
in Martin McDonagh's 2008 dark comedy action

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.230
film In Bruges.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:29.280
The movie features Farrell in a Golden Globe-winning
performance as Ray, a hitman who retreats

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.220
with his mentor Ken to Bruges, Belgium, after
a hit gone wrong.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:34.980
"You two are weird.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:38.400
Would you like some cocaine?"

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:43.380
The movie, which earned an Oscar nomination
for Best Original Screenplay, also features

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:48.459
great supporting performances from Ralph Fiennes
as Ray's boss Harry and Clemence Poesy as

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:50.440
his love interest Chloe.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.760
Although there are plenty of funny moments,
the movie is really a story about redemption,

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:59.110
slipping a strong message, and a surprisingly
insightful examination of mortality, under

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.870
the veil of humor.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.489
Ingrid Goes West

00:03:02.489 --> 00:03:07.430
Aubrey Plaza's Instagram envy goes off the
rails in Ingrid Goes West, which features

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:12.050
the former Parks and Recreation star as Ingrid,
a troubled young woman who decides to move

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:16.370
out west and befriend L.A. socialite Taylor,
played by Elizabeth Olsen.

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:20.739
They quickly forge a bond, but the facade
soon begins to crack, leading to a darkly

00:03:20.739 --> 00:03:22.030
funny conclusion.

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:26.730
Ingrid Goes West definitely pushes the boundaries
of comedy, blurring the line between personal

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.260
trauma and dark humor.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:33.400
While the movie features impressive back-up
performances from Olsen, O'Shea Jackson Jr.,

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.680
and Wyatt Russell, it's Plaza who really shines,
showing that her acting range goes far beyond

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:40.290
Park's April Ludgate.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:44.209
Ingrid Goes West will make you laugh, but
with Plaza at the helm, it'll also give you

00:03:44.209 --> 00:03:45.700
all the feels.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.629
"What's your biggest emotional wound?"

00:03:47.629 --> 00:03:48.629
"What?"

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:51.970
"It's our question of the day."

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:53.250
What We Do in the Shadows

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.420
"When you're a vampire, you become very sexy."

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:04.780
Taika Waititi's What We Do in the Shadows
is a vampire movie for people who hate vampire

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:05.780
movies.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:10.310
The film follows the movements of four vampire
roommates, played by Waititi, Jemaine Clement,

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:15.069
Jonathan Brugh, and Ben Fransham, as seen
through the lens of a documentary crew.

00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:19.190
The four vampires in question all live together,
and they have the same conflicts that any

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.639
human roommates would have.

00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:24.770
"The point is, Deacon, that you have not done
the dishes for five years."

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:29.370
"That is right, it's unacceptable to have
so many bloody dishes all over this bench

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:30.370
like that."

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:34.340
Things get even more tense for the roommates
when they have to deal with the newly "turned"

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.600
Nick, whose reckless behavior threatens to
expose their secrets.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:42.280
Putting a human touch on the film makes the
movie a very different take on the vampire

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.490
genre, and Waititi's always on point sense
of humor makes it a coffin full of laughs

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.300
from start to finish.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.300
Slither

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:54.060
Written and directed by Guardians of the Galaxy's
James Gunn, the horror comedy Slither features

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:58.620
a group of small-town residents dealing with
the sudden appearance of an alien parasite

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:01.151
that has the ability to take over people's
bodies and minds.

00:05:01.151 --> 00:05:04.780
"Oh my God, baby, what happened to your face?"

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.860
"It's just a bee sting."

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:13.720
Fans of Guardians of the Galaxy will be familiar
with the film's antagonist, Michael Rooker,

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:15.900
who plays Yondu in the MCU.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:19.020
Rooker is incredible as the infected Grant
Grant.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:24.220
Elizabeth Banks costars, providing Rooker
solid back-up as his clever wife Starla.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:28.840
The movie also features an impressive performance
from the always charming Nathan Fillion, making

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:32.660
it a thoroughly enjoyable — if pretty damn
gross — horror ride.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:33.970
Thanks for watching!

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:36.720
